From 3515631840e68bafd5ea8e19f6d0f99ffdeb88ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1aeo <github@1aeo.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 02:38:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/20] dos: Count HSDir requests from unknown previous hops

Tor builds the circuit of every anonymized directory request, including
each onion service descriptor fetch and upload, through relays in the
consensus, and so does Arti. Nothing counts how often an HSDir sees
otherwise.

Count the onion service directory requests over an anonymous circuit,
and the first HSDir request on it, whose previous hop is neither in our
consensus nor described by a descriptor we have, as RefuseUnknownExits
checks for exit streams, and export them as
tor_relay_dos_total{type="hsdir_unknown_prev_hop"}. They are a share of
the requests in tor_relay_hsdir_fetch_total and
tor_relay_hsdir_upload_total that are neither single_hop nor refused as
a second HSDir request on their circuit. Nothing is refused. The cost is
one known-relay lookup per such request. directory_handle_command_post()
grows by a line: raise its practracker exception to 139.

Part of #41339.
